<title>USA: Paul Harris prepays $14.7 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Paul Harris prepays $14.7 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paul Harris Stores Inc said Wednesday it has prepaid the remaining $14.7 million of notes issued on September 15, 1992.</p>
<p>The prepayment lowered the specialty apparel retailer's long-term debt-to-equity ratio to 0.05 from 0.54, Paul Harris said.</p>
<p>The notes were due in semiannual installments with final payment on January 31, 2000.</p>
<p>There was no prepayment penalty, Paul Harris said.</p>
<p>Paul Harris shares were up 7/8 at 21 Wednesday.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
